            <ArticleTitle>Comfort measures: practical care of the dying cancer patient.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>488-93</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1177/1049909110380200</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Most patients with advanced malignancy will die of their disease. Care of the dying is therefore a fundamental skill for the oncologist. Although protocols exist in other countries, there is no established protocol in the United States. We present a protocol for management of the dying that is clinically useful and review the existing evidence-base.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
